#!/usr/bin/env -S python3 -I
"""rahbot: the Riemann@home v1 bot. Checks volunteers' build records and keeps data.json.
Two proofs (CONTRACT "Several proofs"): 17M (the original) and 300K (grh-lean, readable edition); see PROOFS.

Spec: ../../shardcheck/CONTRACT.md (formats + acceptance rules). Python 3 stdlib only; run with `python3 -I`.
One PR per computer (build): it adds submissions/<login>/<build_id>.json and the volunteer's tool overwrites that
file on the same branch every ~10 min. The bot checks each new version against that build's last accepted version,
shows accepted versions of open PRs in data.json without merging, and merges only when the accepted version is whole or final
(CONTRACT "No stale merge": one PR per build for life; abandoned PRs simply stay open).

Commands
  rahbot check RECORD.json --author LOGIN --prev PREV.json|none [--path submissions/LOGIN/BUILD_ID.json]
               [--check-digest [--reference-hashes SNAP]]
      Apply every CONTRACT acceptance rule. PREV = this build's last accepted version. Prints ACCEPT / REJECT /
      PENDING with reasons and FLAG lines. Exit 0 accept, 1 reject, 2 pending (digest rule on, reference lacks modules).
  rahbot reference-digest BITMAP [--reference-hashes SNAP]
      olean_digest the reference build (/Users/Shared/riemann-at-home/lean, read-only) gives for BITMAP
      (a record JSON, or a file holding the bitmap_b64 text).
  rahbot reference-snapshot --out SNAP
      Freeze sha256 of every reference .olean (32 bytes x N, zeros = not compiled) so digests don't move while
      the reference build is still running.
  rahbot aggregate DIR [DIR ...] --out data.json
      data.json from accepted records laid out as DIR/<login>/<build_id>.json (repo submissions/ = merged builds,
      STATE/accepted/ = accepted versions of open PRs). Newest version per build wins; each is re-checked.
  rahbot poll --repo OWNER/NAME --workdir CLONE [--state DIR] [--live]
      One pass (launchd runs it every 10 min). Without --live: prints decisions, writes nothing, calls only
      read-only gh (GraphQL list + file contents). --live: comments, closes, merges, commits + pushes data.json.
  rahbot poll --fixtures DIR --round K --workdir SCRATCH
      Same logic over DIR/rounds.json[K-1] (fake PRs, fake clock); SCRATCH/repo plays main, SCRATCH/state the
      bot state; round 1 starts fresh. Never calls gh or git.
"""
